  <constraints>
    <constraint source="owner Q4">Scope: every enforcement point in this task. For INTERNAL users (systemusers) the wall is enforced on SECURE records (`sprk_issecure` = true via `ExternalParticipationService.GetRootRecordFlagsAsync` `:541`), and on their child records once C10 part 2 (task 146 and its client-side sibling) makes children secure. On non-secure records nothing in this task adds a wall on internal access; the one change there is the parity correction of escalation (h), applied only per the owner's answer. Contact-plane behaviour (FR-23 for contacts everywhere) is unchanged.</constraint>
    <constraint source="subject match (per escalations (a) and (b))">Scope: the guard, the enforcer and the veto. A systemuser is walled when an ACTIVE entry's subject is:
(i) the systemuser itself (`sprk_subjectsystemuser`);
(ii) the user's linked contact via 141;
(iii) an organization the linked contact is an active member of.
The entry's object must be the secure record itself, a child record of it, or an organization the secure record references. Record-side organizations are ANY referenced org, not just registry ones — FR-23 / B-10 over-match, reusing `GetReferencedOrganizationIdsAsync` (`ExternalParticipationService.cs:710`).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-003 fail closed">Scope: guard + enforcer + veto.
- An unreadable deny list, flag set, link or org membership at share-write time → the share is REFUSED with a message.
- In the veto → the record is removed.
- In the enforcer → the run is recorded failed and nothing is reported "clean".
Never treat a fault as "not walled".</constraint>
    <constraint source="refusal contract">Scope: InternalShareEndpoints.ShareAsync and every other guarded share site. A walled target is refused BEFORE any Dataverse write, as 403 ProblemDetails with a new stable reason code (e.g. `sdap.access.user_share.subject_no_access`) and a human message saying the person is on the No Access list for this record. The message does not reveal the entry's reason text. The refusal is logged with the entry id(s).</constraint>
    <constraint source="enforcer">Scope: the enforce endpoint, the job and task 064's add path.
- Removes only DIRECT POA shares to the walled systemuser on covered secure records, via `IDataverseRecordShareService.RevokeAccessAsync` with a strict read before and a read-back after (the `InternalShareEndpoints.UnshareAsync` discipline, `:395-486`: strict read `:440`, revoke `:464`, read-back `:465`, failure → message `:477-486`).
- A removed share that was a task-142 auto share is left for 142's ledger to record as Skipped(no-access), not Declined (142 wires this; if 142 has not landed, the notes name the hook).
- Invalidates the user's impersonated root-set cache (`ImpersonatedRootSetSource.InvalidateAsync`, as `InternalShareEndpoints.cs:358-359` / `:473-474` do) under the SAME tenant key `ImpersonatedRootSetSource.GetAsync` reads. In the job (no caller) that key comes from the deployment's tenant configuration, never `CacheTenantFor(null)` = "anonymous".
- Never revokes a TEAM share, team ownership, or role-conferred access. Those are REPORTED as "wall not enforceable in Dataverse for user X on record Y via Z" in the endpoint response, the job result and a Warning log. The policy follows escalation (d).</constraint>
    <constraint source="deploy order">Scope: rollout. The `sprk_subjectsystemuser` column is created live (Spaarke publisher, SpaarkeCore — the Web-API method in the schema doc :180-204) and verified with describe() BEFORE any code that selects it is deployed. Record the order in the PR description. A reader that selects a missing column fails closed into a deny-all outage.</constraint>
    <constraint source="D-1 / ADR-002 / ADR-036 / ADR-052">Scope: triggers. No plugin, flow or service endpoint. The job is an `IScheduledJob` registered with `AddScheduledJob` in `ExternalAccessModule`, following `ExternalAccessReconciliationJob`'s A1 rules (claim → check → write → marker; paging ceiling reports TRUNCATED; failure recorded, never "nothing to reconcile"). Posture and cadence per escalation (e).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-003 / ADR-008 — enforce endpoint">Scope: `POST .../no-access/enforce`.
- The body carries ONLY the entry id. Everything else is read server-side from the active entry; any other field is ignored.
- It joins the `/api/v1/external-access` group, so `DelegationRuleFilter` gates it. Add a case for the enforce request type to the filter's target switch (`DelegationRuleFilter.cs:211-281`) whose target is the `sprk_noaccessentries` row itself, so the filter's existing caller-OBO Write check applies to the entry. An absent entry, or one the caller cannot write, is the filter's 403 (`:144-179`), indistinguishable from each other — not a 404 from the handler.
- An inactive entry reaches the handler and is refused with ProblemDetails and no writes.
- The endpoint can only REMOVE access, and only as far as an existing active entry says. It accelerates what the job would do on its next run; it never grants.
- Which entries the enforcer honours at all follows escalation (g).</constraint>
    <constraint source="CLAUDE.md §11 reuse">Scope: whole task. Extend `NoAccessListReader` (do not add a second deny reader). Reuse `ExternalParticipationService.GetRootRecordFlagsAsync` (`:541`), `GetReferencedOrganizationIdsAsync` (`:710`), `QueryActiveOrgIdsAsync` (`:1081`), 141's link resolver and `IDataverseRecordShareService`. Task 142 consumes the guard; it does not fork one.</constraint>
    <constraint source="owner directives (binding)">Scope: whole task.
- A failed revoke/unshare returns a message, never a bare 500.
- No new `.WithClientSecret`.
- `GrantMembershipAsync` stays at zero callers.
- Users are not relocated between BUs.
- No Dataverse test in CI: live proof is the MANUAL gate.</constraint>
    <constraint source="CLAUDE.md §10">Scope: this task's PR. Placement statement against bff-extensions.md. Publish size: fresh-master vs fresh-branch worktrees at short paths, Compress-Archive, both sizes + delta + both file counts, ≤ 60 MB. No new HIGH CVE.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038">Scope: tests. No `Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt;`, no DI-registration tests, no ctor null-check tests. Use the reader's `QueryChunkAsync` override seam and the existing share-service test doubles.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <justification>
    <existing>(1) Column: `sprk_noaccessentry` has only `sprk_subjectcontact` / `sprk_subjectorganization` (entity-schema.md:58-61). `rg "_sprk_subject" src/server` hits only `NoAccessListReader.cs:181`. (2) Guard/enforcer: `InternalShareEndpoints.ShareAsync` checks eligibility (`:251`) and caller rights (`:290-303`) but no deny list. `ResolveDenyVetoAsync` (`AccessibleRecordSetService.cs:596`) is read-time only and contact-keyed. Nothing revokes a share because of a wall. (3) Job: `ExternalAccessReconciliationJob` R1-R3 repair grant/membership row lifecycle; `GrantExpiryReminderJob` sends reminders. Neither reads POA shares. (4) Enforce endpoint: task 064's planned deny-list add endpoint (pending) is the only other trigger, and it cannot see entries authored on the MDA form. (5) Web resource: `sprk_kpiassessment_quickcreate.js` is the only OnPostSave→BFF caller, and it is KPI-specific.</existing>
    <extension>(1) Relying on the linked contact instead of a new column: rejected as primary (see escalation (a)). 7 of 8 dev users have no link today, and a wall that depends on data hygiene fails OPEN when the link is missing. (2) The guard is a new class used by ≥4 share sites, so each site calls it rather than each re-implementing the rule. The read-time veto extends `ResolveDenyVetoAsync`. (3) Adding an R4 to `ExternalAccessReconciliationJob` was rejected: that job's contract is row lifecycle of grant/membership rows (:16-19). It ships disabled/report-only (D-2 part 3), which would leave the owner's wall un-enforced for out-of-band shares. (4) The enforce endpoint joins the existing `/api/v1/external-access` group.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>(1) When 036's flag turns on, a walled internal attorney who holds (or is later given, by OOB Share or /share-user) a share on a secure matter reads it in MDA AND Teams/SPA. The owner's No Access List then binds contacts only, directly contradicting Q4. (2) Without the write-time guard, /share-user and task 142's auto-share hand a walled user access that the next read-time veto only partly hides (MDA would still admit them). (3) Without the enforcer, an entry added after a share exists changes nothing in Dataverse. (4) Without the job, an OOB MDA share made after the entry stays in place indefinitely.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

