  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">1. `sprk_subjectsystemuser` exists live and was verified by describe() before the code deployed (order recorded). The schema doc states exactly-one-of-three subjects. The reader treats a row with zero or ≥2 subjects as malformed: it denies nothing and logs a warning.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">2. Given an active entry (subject = systemuser U, object = secure project P), when a caller with Write on P calls /share-user for U, then the response is 403 ProblemDetails with the new reason code and a human message, and NO Dataverse share write occurs (asserted).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">3. The same refusal holds when the entry's subject is U's 141-linked contact. It also holds when the subject is an organization U's linked contact actively belongs to (per (b)). It also holds when the object is an organization P references via ANY lookup.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">4. On a NON-secure record, the same entry does NOT block /share-user for U (the owner's scope). Contact grants behave exactly as before this task.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">5. Fail closed: when the deny list, P's flags, U's link or U's org memberships cannot be read at share time, /share-user refuses with a message and writes nothing.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">6. Given U already holds a direct POA share on secure project P, when an entry walling U off P is saved (form post-save → enforce endpoint), then U's direct share is revoked and confirmed gone by read-back, U's impersonated root-set cache is invalidated under the key a read for U uses, and the response lists what was removed. A read-back that still finds the share → ProblemDetails with a message naming the user and record, never a bare 500 and never "removed".</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">7. Access held through a team share, team ownership or a role is NOT revoked. It is reported as not enforceable in Dataverse, with the user, the record and the mechanism (policy per (d)).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">8. Enforce endpoint authorization, tested THROUGH the real `/api/v1/external-access` filter pipeline (not by calling the handler directly). A caller with Write on an active entry reaches the handler and the enforcement runs — this proves the new `DelegationRuleFilter` case resolves the enforce request type (without it the default branch denies everyone). Unauthenticated → 401. An entry that does not exist, and one the caller cannot write, → the filter's 403, identical to each other, no writes. An inactive entry → ProblemDetails with a message, no writes. A body with extra fields (record or user ids) is ignored in favour of the entry's own data. A revoke fault → ProblemDetails with a message, never a bare 500.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">8a. Per escalation (g): with the recommendation, an entry whose last modifier lacks Write on object record R removes NOTHING on R and reports "not enforced: author lacks Write on record" for R (endpoint, job and 064 add path), while the read-time veto for R still applies. With the alternative, the notes record the live role privileges on `sprk_noaccessentry` before and after, showing only the governance role can create/write entries.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">9. Provisioning follows the owner's answer to (c). With the recommendation: a walled creator is refused before the ownership move, with nothing moved. A walled named principal is skipped with a per-principal warning, and the other principals are still shared.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">10. Every census share site on secure records calls the guard before writing (a test per site). Non-secure sites are recorded in the notes with evidence. Task 142's auto-share consumes the same guard, or the notes name the exact hook 142 must call if 142 has not yet landed. The same holds for task 149's child-share fan-out and for `DirectThreadAccessService` on a communication under a secure parent: guarded here if already secure-child sites when this task runs, otherwise the notes name the hook and the orchestrator is told.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">11. Teams/SPA plane: a systemuser U walled off secure record P (by any subject form in criteria 2-3) does not have P in the composed set, even when a membership or grant term would otherwise add it. A non-secure record is never removed by a systemuser-subject entry. For a linked-contact or org entry on a non-secure record, the result follows the owner's answer to (h) (with the recommendation: U keeps the record at the systemuser's own non-contact term's rights, and the linked contact's grant contribution is vetoed — test both halves). A veto-read fault removes the candidate.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">12. The job removes a direct share created out of band (e.g. OOB MDA Share) after an entry exists. It also enforces on records that became secure after the entry and on users whose 141 link appeared after the entry. Every share it removes invalidates U's root-set cache under the tenant key `ImpersonatedRootSetSource.GetAsync` reads (test asserts the key; "anonymous" fails the test). Paging past its ceiling reports TRUNCATED. A faulted run records Success=false. Posture and cadence per (e).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">13. Test scope: cover the stated contract plus the edge cases named in criteria 1-12 (three subject forms, org object over-match, secure vs non-secure, the (h) split, fail-closed reads, team/role non-removable, provisioning creator vs named principal, endpoint negatives through the filter, entry-author authority, job transitions, job cache key). No criterion is met by a test that only asserts a mock was called with arguments the test itself supplied. Anything beyond that needs a one-line justification in the notes. No ADR-038-banned test shapes. Build, full BFF unit suite and ArchTests green. Publish size reported (fresh-master vs fresh-branch, sizes, delta, zip tool, file counts) ≤ 60 MB. No new HIGH CVE. No new `.WithClientSecret`. No plugin or flow.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">14. MANUAL live gate on spaarkedev1, using the existing non-admin test users in their current BUs (no relocation), with the evidence recorded:
(i) confirm U cannot open the secure project before any share (recorded); share it to U via Manage Access "+ User"; U opens it in MDA and Teams/SPA;
(ii) add a No Access entry naming U (systemuser subject) on that project in MDA; after save, U can open it in neither MDA nor Teams/SPA, and the share is gone from Manage Access;
(iii) "+ User" for U on that project now shows the refusal message;
(iv) deactivating the entry does NOT restore the MANUAL share, which stays removed until re-granted deliberately (a task-142 auto share is restored by 142's invariant instead — not part of this gate);
(v) with a second active entry in place, an administrator shares the project to U through the OOB MDA Share dialog; after the next job run U can open it in neither MDA nor Teams/SPA.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <ui-tests>
    <test name="+ User refusal shows the reason">
      <steps>
        <step>At https://{org}.crm.dynamics.com, as a non-admin test user with Write on a secure project, open Manage Access and try "+ User" for a user who is on that project's No Access list.</step>
      </steps>
      <expected>The modal shows the server's message ("on the No Access list for this record"), not a generic error, and the user does not appear in Current Access.</expected>
    </test>
    <test name="Saving a No Access entry removes the share">
      <steps>
        <step>Create a sprk_noaccessentry in MDA naming a systemuser who currently holds a share on a secure project; save.</step>
        <step>Reopen the project's Manage Access.</step>
      </steps>
      <expected>The user's share is gone, and the form did not error during save.</expected>
    </test>
  </ui-tests>

  <notes>Defect C9 (notes/session26-uac-defects-and-synopsis.md §C9); owner round 2 item 5(a) and Q4 (notes/session27-owner-decisions-and-research.md:24, :33); live link fact session27:40. Coordination the orchestrator must act on:
- task 064's deny-list add/remove endpoints (POML :23) are keyed contact|organization only. They must accept the systemuser subject and call this task's enforcer on add.
- task 067's Manage Access deny section must offer a user picker and render the "not enforceable in Dataverse" state from (d).
- task 142 depends on this task's guard, and records a share this task's enforcer removed as Skipped(no-access), so a lifted wall restores an Assigned auto share while a manual share stays removed.
- task 149 (C10 sharees) must call this task's guard before any child-share fan-out and let the enforcer remove walled users' child shares, if 149 lands after this task.
- task 036 depends on this task; escalations (d) and (h) decide where the BFF veto and Dataverse may disagree, which 036's own escalation trigger checks.
Deactivating an entry lifts the veto (schema Business Rule 2) but does not re-create removed shares. Removal is not reversible by design; restoring access is a deliberate re-grant. Say so in the schema doc.</notes>

