    <outcome date="2026-10-02" branch="task/uac-r2-143" base="7128776b7">
SERVER SIDE CODE-COMPLETE; LIVE GATES PENDING; FORM STEPS RECORDED FOR TASK 154. Full record: notes/task-143-no-access-internal-secure.md (owner answers, census, placement + justification, tests, bite proof, pending gates, residuals).

OWNER ANSWERS APPLIED (no escalation fired as a stop): (a)=N1 systemuser column + linked contact; (b)=N4 organization subjects bind members (own-firm warning = 067's dialog); (c)=N6 walled creator refused before the move, walled colleagues skipped and reported, walled resume person refused; (d)=N2 team/role/BU access reported, never revoked, hidden on Teams/SPA (section 6.5 path A, recorded in design.md section 9); (e)=R4 job enabled, writes on, every 5 minutes; (g)=N5 a record is enforced only when the entry's modifiedby is an enabled person holding Write on it; (h)=N3 non-secure: user-subject entries do nothing, contact/org entries remove only the linked contact's contribution; S5 the last person is kept; O2 answered (access-administrator role) but its application is 154/064's. Trigger (f) does not fire: DirectThreadAccessService can consult the guard internally (hook recorded for 146/149).

BUILT: sprk_subjectsystemuser (schema doc + scripts/Set-NoAccessSystemUserSubjectSchema.ps1, dry-run/-Apply/-Verify); NoAccessListReader three-subject overload, exactly-one-of-three rule, DenyingSubjectKinds; SecureShareNoAccessGuard (the one write-time check) wired into /share-user and secure provisioning; NoAccessEnforcementStore + NoAccessShareEnforcer (EnforceEntryAsync, EnforceForRecordAsync for 142's Update Access); POST /api/v1/external-access/no-access/enforce with its DelegationRuleFilter case (target = the entry row); NoAccessShareReconciliationJob (AddScheduledJob, ADR-036/052); systemuser-plane veto split by secure; ImpersonatedRootSetSource deployment-tenant invalidation; ExternalParticipationService reverse reads; sprk_noaccessentry_postsave.js (not registered - 154).

PLACEMENT (CLAUDE.md section 10): all in the BFF - BFF domain code over BFF-owned tables, BFF identity, low volume; the job on the in-process scheduler (ADR-052 B2/B3). No new package, no AI-internal type (ADR-013), no new .WithClientSecret, no plugin (ADR-002), GrantMembershipAsync untouched.

THREE-QUESTION JUSTIFICATIONS (CLAUDE.md section 11): column - only contact/org subjects exist, linked-contact-only fails OPEN for unlinked users; guard - IsGranteeDeniedOnRecordAsync covers contacts only and the evaluator's link read is not status-bearing, and 4+ sites need one rule; store - DataverseWebApiClient cannot call RetrievePrincipalAccess and CallerRecordAccessProbe is OBO-only by design, while N5 and criterion 7 need it for another principal; enforcer - nothing removes a share because of a wall; endpoint - 064 cannot see MDA-authored entries and R3 requires save-time; job - ExternalAccessReconciliationJob's reason to change is grant/membership row lifecycle and it ships disabled; reverse reads and cache-tenant helper are extensions of their owning classes. Table in notes section 3.

TESTS: guard 16, enforcer 19, endpoint through the real filter pipeline with the DI-composed enforcer 8, job 8, provisioning 5, reader +9, evaluator 4 (one rewritten to the owner's N3 answer), /share-user +10. Ten guards seeded at once - 27 tests failed, each seed its own - restored and touched.

PENDING MANUAL GATES (main session): G-1 schema -Apply then -Verify BEFORE any BFF deploy of this branch (the reader selects _sprk_subjectsystemuser_value; without the column every No Access read fails closed - deny-all on both planes); G-2 BFF deploy; G-3 task 154 form registration (bff_auth.js first); G-4 live gate 14 (needs O2 applied first - the O2 trigger).

HOOKS FOR OTHER TASKS: 142 (call the guard before every Assigned-To share; ledger an enforcer-removed share as Skipped(no-access); Update Access calls EnforceForRecordAsync); 149 (guard with the ROOT before any child share; extend the enforcer to child shares); 146/149 (DirectThreadAccessService on a message under a secure root); 064 (accept the systemuser subject; enforce after add; create the entry AS THE CALLER or N5 sees the app user as author); 067 (user picker; own-firm warning; render not-enforceable); 036 (the N2 disagreement is bounded to NotEnforceable cases).
    </outcome>
    <outcome date="2026-10-03" branch="task/uac-r2-143-r1" base="d248dff11" round="r1">
ROUND r1 - ADVERSARIAL-VERIFIER FINDINGS CLOSED (server side). Full record: notes/task-143-no-access-internal-secure.md section 7. Live writes: none.

ITEM 2 (MEDIUM, fail-open) FIXED, section 6.5 path C (comply, ADR-003): for every SECURE candidate the systemuser-plane veto resolves its subjects through the write-time guard's static SecureShareNoAccessGuard.ResolveSubjectsAsync over IContactIdentityStore, read status-first (systemuser + sprk_primarycontact link + every oid-bound contact + their wall organizations, plus the principal's derived contact). A faulted link, binding or membership read removes every secure candidate whole. Non-secure candidates keep the N3 rule over the derived contact only (a contact the normalizer could not derive contributed no grant, so nothing opens). Residual W4 withdrawn.
ITEM 3 FIXED by item 2; the guard's remark rewritten to state exactly who asks what.
ITEM 4 CLOSED: one test per untested seed, each on the PRODUCTION fault shape - S1 guard and S18 EnforceForRecordAsync with ReferencedOrganizations.Unresolved returned (never thrown); S2 flags IsUnreadable with IsSecure false (RootRecordFlags.Unreadable also sets IsSecure, which is why the verifier's seed was inert against production values); S9 membership read faulting on a non-secure record; S11 owner read throwing; S20 colleague link read failing -> skipped with principal_no_access_unverifiable.
ITEM 5 FIXED: every referenced organization is queried, in OR-chunks of 50, answers unioned, Truncated past max.
ITEM 6 FIXED: direct-share removal runs under a per-record lease (the existing atomic IScheduledJobLease, keyed no-access-enforce:{table}:{id}, 2 min) and re-reads the shares under it before the S5 check, revoke and read-back; held lease -> record-busy, unreachable -> record-lock-unavailable (fail closed, nothing removed). Scope: serializes the enforcer with itself (endpoint, concurrent endpoint calls, job); task 139's unshare and the MDA Share dialog do not take it.
ITEM 7 FIXED: the scan pages every active entry id (nextLink, ceiling 50,000 -> TRUNCATED); at most 500 enforced per run, the window ROTATES from an in-instance cursor so every entry is enforced within ceil(N/500) runs (reported ROTATING, status partial).
ITEM 8 no change: the test asserts the shipped cron/enabled VALUES (owner R4), not a registration; perturbing either reddens it.
ITEMS 10-12 (criteria 11, 13, 9) now met and tested. ITEMS 13-14 (criteria 1, 14) NOT CLOSABLE HERE: live gates G-1 (schema -Apply then -Verify, BEFORE any BFF deploy of this branch) and gate 14 (after G-1, G-2 deploy, task 154 form registration, O2 applied) remain the main session's.

PEER REPORT #1081 (owner 2026-10-02): no code change. In dev a walled root-team member's secure-record access is role-or-business-unit (reported NotEnforceable, hidden on Teams/SPA, never revoked); live gate 14 must use child-BU users.

PLACEMENT / JUSTIFICATION (CLAUDE.md sections 10/11): no new service, endpoint, DI registration, option, job, column or package. Extensions only: AccessibleRecordSetService and NoAccessShareEnforcer each take one already-registered singleton (IContactIdentityStore; IScheduledJobLease - reused, not a new lock primitive: Existing = the scheduler's atomic lease and IIdempotencyService; Extension = the lease is atomic and fails loudly, while IIdempotencyService's lock is check-then-set and fails OPEN on a cache fault, unusable for S5; Cost of doing nothing = two concurrent enforcements can remove a secure record's last two readers, violating owner S5). NoAccessEnforcementStore gains two internal wire seams (QueryActiveEntryIdsAsync, ReadActiveEntryIdPageAsync); SecureShareNoAccessGuard's subject resolution becomes a shared static.

TESTS: r1 adds evaluator 4, guard 1, enforcer 5, store 5 (new NoAccessEnforcementStoreTests), job 2, provisioning 1 = 18; task-related set 537/537. Bite proof: 13 violations seeded one at a time (build + the 537 task tests each), every one reddening its own new test(s), restored and touched: B1 veto ignores a faulted link read (1); B2 veto back to the derived contact only (2); S1 (1); S18 (1); S2 (1); S9 (1); S11 (1); S20 (1); L1 removal without the record lock (3); L2 proceeding when the lease store is unreachable (1); C1 first 50 organizations only (1); P1 one scan page only (2); J1 same first window every run (1). Full suite and ArchTests: BFF build 0 errors 0 warnings; full BFF unit suite 14423 passed, 0 failed, 54 skipped, 14477 total (20m48s; the verifier's 14405 + the 18 new); Spaarke.ArchTests 346/346. Publish size not measured (main session)..
