    <outcome date="2026-10-03" branch="task/uac-r2-143-r2" base="a4ade61a8" round="r2">
ROUND r2 - ADVERSARIAL-VERIFIER FINDINGS CLOSED (server side). Full record: notes/task-143-no-access-internal-secure.md section 8. Live writes: none.

ITEM 1 (MEDIUM) CLOSED: new test AnEnforcementWhoseFirstShareReadPredatesAnotherEnforcementsRemoval_ReReadsUnderTheLock_AndKeepsTheLastReader. Enforcement B reads the shares {Walled, walledToo} BEFORE enforcement A takes the lock. A then runs start to finish and releases. B takes the free lock, re-reads, keeps walledToo's share (last-person-on-secure-record) and reports no failure, so the re-read, not the lock, decides. The verifier's exact seed (lock taken, stale pre-lock shares used) reddens this test alone. The r1 bite row L1 proves the lock only; this is corrected in the notes.

ITEM 2 (LOW-MEDIUM) SURFACED, section 6.5 path A, PROPOSED and NOT YET ACCEPTED. The tension is the enforcer reusing IScheduledJobLease (the scheduler's dispatch-lease store) as a per-record mutex, which NoAccessShareReconciliationJob reaches transitively, against ADR-036 A1-7 / ADR-052 section 5. It is recorded as a new row in design.md section 9 and named in the enforcer's ctor doc. The second key site is catalogued under SystemCacheKeys.SchedulerLease (raw key {InstanceName}scheduler:lease:no-access-enforce:{table}:{recordId}); no new allow-list entry. Path C was rejected because IIdempotencyService's lock is check-then-set and fails OPEN, and a new lock type would duplicate RedisScheduledJobLease. Path B was rejected because the rule's intent holds. ESCALATION: the reviewer must accept or decline explicitly, and the task-143 PR must cite the design.md section 9 row.

ITEM 3 (LOW) FIXED: the removal lease is RENEWED immediately before the revoke. A renewal answering false (expired, or held by someone else) removes nothing and reports record-lock-lost. A renewal that throws removes nothing and reports record-lock-unavailable. RecordLockDuration 2 -&gt; 5 min, so it outlasts the revoke's client bound (100 s HTTP timeout + 30 s token wait). Residual stated in notes section 6: a revoke Dataverse applies after the client gave up, later than 5 min after the renewal; not closable without fencing.

ITEM 4 (LOW) CLOSED: the URL choice is extracted unchanged into internal static NoAccessEnforcementStore.ResolveRequestUrl, which GetAsync calls. Eight cases cover a relative path, two links under the root, and five refused links (another host, a look-alike host, another version, a bare-prefix root, an http downgrade). Scan-level behaviour is unchanged and documented: a refused link fails the run (status error) and never enforces a silent prefix.

ITEM 5 (TRIVIAL) FIXED: NeverDeniesReader's summary moved back to its method.

ITEMS 6-10: verified or accepted, no change. ITEMS 11-12 (criterion 13): the test half is now met; the publish-size report stays with the main session. ITEMS 13-14 (criteria 1, 14) NOT CLOSABLE HERE. Live gate G-1: pwsh scripts/Set-NoAccessSystemUserSubjectSchema.ps1 -EnvironmentUrl https://spaarkedev1.crm.dynamics.com -Apply, then -Verify (exit 0) and describe('tables/sprk_noaccessentry'), BEFORE any BFF deploy of this branch. Gate 14 runs after G-1, G-2 (BFF deploy), task 154's form registration (bff_auth.js before noaccessentry_postsave.js) and O2 applied. It uses child-BU users only, never root-BU or Spaarke Demo team members (#1081, round 5).

PLACEMENT / JUSTIFICATION (CLAUDE.md sections 10/11): no new service, endpoint, DI registration, option, job, column or package. Extensions only: NoAccessShareEnforcer gains a private RenewRecordLockAsync and a longer RecordLockDuration. NoAccessEnforcementStore gains internal static ResolveRequestUrl, extracted from GetAsync without changing behaviour. The SystemCacheKeys.SchedulerLease doc names its second site; the entry count is unchanged.

TESTS: r2 adds enforcer 3 and store 8 = 11. The task-related set is 356/356. Bite proof: 5 violations seeded one at a time (build, then the 356 task tests), each restored from a backup and touched: L3 stale shares under the lock (1 failed), R1 no renewal (2), R2 a lost renewal treated as held (1), U1 no origin check (5), U2 a bare-prefix origin check (1). Full BFF unit suite 14434 passed / 0 failed / 54 skipped (14488 total); Spaarke.ArchTests 346/346; build 0 errors / 0 warnings. Publish size: main session.
